### ===================================
### PART 2: CRUD operations
### ===================================

### 7) List all questions (admin view - includes answers)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/questions
Accept: application/json


### 8) Get one question by ID
GET http://localhost:8080/api/questions/1
Accept: application/json


### 9) Update a question (change question 3)
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/questions/3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "questionText": "What does CSS stand for?",
  "optionA": "Cascading Style Sheets",
  "optionB": "Computer Style Sheets",
  "optionC": "Creative Style System",
  "optionD": "Colorful Style Sheets",
  "correctOption": "A",
  "category": "Technology"
}


### 10) Delete a question
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/questions/6
Accept: application/json


### ===================================
### PART 3: Take a quiz!
### ===================================

### 11) Start a quiz with 3 random questions (no answers shown!)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/quiz/start?count=3
Accept: application/json


### 12) Start a quiz with default count (5 questions)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/quiz/start
Accept: application/json


### 13) Submit answers and get your score
### (Use the question IDs you got from the start endpoint)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/quiz/submit
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "questionId": 1, "selectedOption": "C" },
  { "questionId": 2, "selectedOption": "B" },
  { "questionId": 3, "selectedOption": "A" },
  { "questionId": 4, "selectedOption": "A" },
  { "questionId": 5, "selectedOption": "C" }
]


### 14) Submit answers - get some wrong on purpose
POST http://localhost:8080/api/quiz/submit
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "questionId": 1, "selectedOption": "A" },
  { "questionId": 2, "selectedOption": "A" },
  { "questionId": 4, "selectedOption": "D" }
]


